From 2d85e4f1f25afde2211bb7fa897f23e7f8241069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Silas=20M=C3=BCller?= <dev@silasmueller.de>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:16:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] vhost_user: support VIRTIO Shared Memory Regions in the
 generic device

The vhost-user specification lets a backend expose host memory to the
guest through VIRTIO Shared Memory Regions: the frontend asks for the
region sizes with VHOST_USER_GET_SHMEM_CONFIG once
VHOST_USER_PROTOCOL_F_SHMEM is negotiated, backs the regions, and maps
file descriptors into them on VHOST_USER_BACKEND_SHMEM_MAP and
VHOST_USER_BACKEND_SHMEM_UNMAP. v53.0 has the device plumbing (the cache,
get_shm_regions, userspace_mappings) but never negotiates the feature,
so the generic device never gets regions.

vhost 0.16 cannot express the feature: it defines SHMEM as bit 21, which
the specification assigns to VHOST_USER_PROTOCOL_F_GPA_ADDRESSES. SHMEM
is bit 22. vhost 0.17 corrects this (rust-vmm/vhost#367), so the
vhost-user frontend moves to vhost 0.17. vhost 0.17 uses vm-memory 0.18
and the vhost-kern/vDPA code passes vm-memory 0.17 types, so vDPA stays
on vhost 0.16 and the frontend takes 0.17 as `vhost-frontend`. The
vhost-user backend binaries keep vhost 0.16 and vhost-user-backend 0.22.

Negotiation (generic device only):
- Offer VHOST_USER_PROTOCOL_F_SHMEM and
  VHOST_USER_PROTOCOL_F_BACKEND_SEND_FD. The latter is required for the
  backend to pass the file descriptor of a SHMEM_MAP request.
- With SHMEM acked, send VHOST_USER_GET_SHMEM_CONFIG. The array index is
  the shmid and nregions counts the non-zero sizes. Reject nregions above
  256, a count that disagrees with the non-zero sizes, and sizes that are
  not a multiple of the page size.

Regions:
- device_manager backs all regions with one window, placed back to back
  in shmid order and rounded up to a power of two for the BAR. The window
  is an anonymous PROT_NONE mapping registered as a userspace mapping.
- The region list is indexed by shmid; unused shmids are zero-length
  entries. pci_device emits no shared memory capability for them, so
  cap.id equals the shmid.

Backend requests:
- SHMEM_MAP maps the fd at shm_offset of the region named by shmid. The
  range must lie in that region on page boundaries, fd_offset must be
  page aligned, and the range must not overlap an existing mapping.
  flags bit 0 selects read-write, otherwise read-only.
- SHMEM_UNMAP must name exactly one existing mapping. It lays a PROT_NONE
  placeholder back over the range.
- A refused request returns an error, which FrontendReqHandler turns
  into a non-zero reply when REPLY_ACK is negotiated and the backend set
  NEED_REPLY. Success replies zero.
- A device reset drops every mapping.
- A device with regions refuses to be snapshotted: the mappings belong to
  the backend and are not part of its migrated state.

